            "answer": {
              "status": "complete",
              "answer": "For AAPL (Apple Inc.) fiscal 2024, the annual period spans 2023-10-01 to 2024-09-28 (a 52/53-week fiscal year ending late September), with all reported in USD. Revenue was 391,035,000,000 USD — total net sales for the year. Operating income was 123,216,000,000 USD — the profit remaining after cost of sales and operating expenses (R&D and SG&A), i.e., earnings from operations before non-operating items and taxes. Net income was 93,736,000,000 USD — the bottom-line result after non-operating items and income taxes. The distinction: revenue is the top line; operating income captures core operating profitability; net income is the final profit attributable after all other income/expense and taxes. Operating income represents about 31.5% of revenue and net income about 24.0% of revenue. All figures are from the same annual fiscal period, so they are directly comparable.",
